Spoken answer:

In our project, GitHub is used for source code management and Jenkins is used for continuous integration and deployment.

Whenever a developer pushes code into GitHub, a webhook triggers the Jenkins pipeline.

Jenkins checks out the latest source code and performs the build and unit testing.

After successful validation, Jenkins creates Docker images for our .NET frontend and backend applications.

Then Jenkins pushes those images into Amazon ECR.

Finally, our deployment process updates the Docker containers running on EC2.

So GitHub manages our source code, and Jenkins automates the build and deployment process.

